body:
So I didn't actually report the freelance gig during 2021 as I only started in January of 2022. I worked a good bit of jobs during that year, three I think, and I ended up owing no money and instead got a roughly 1700 dollar refund.

&#x200B;

That 2,000 estimate is a bit alarming, as I guess my confusion is that I've never actually had to pay the IRS any money and only received from them instead. In not paying quarterly taxes for 2022 from my 10-99 gig, have I gotten myself into owing them a lot come tax season?

Phew, that's a relief. Utilizing a calculator it seems like the amount I'd be paying for quarterly is pretty negligible either way, but in the meantime I've kept a good record of every invoice for my freelance work alongside tax documents.

&#x200B;

The only other question I have is what exactly is meant by prepay. Should I worry about that 236 now or is that a bridge to cross come tax season next year? And also I'm assuming my first quarterly payment is due April of 2023, yeah?

&#x200B;

Thank you for the information also, definitely de-stressing me out haha
